<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zwentibold</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 870–900</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Zwentibold of Lotharingia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zwentibold was the illegitimate son of the East Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a>, who made him king of Lotharingia in 895. His rule provoked the Lotharingian nobility, led by Reginar, and after Arnulf's death he was killed in battle on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> on 13 August 900. Lotharingia then passed to his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-child">Louis the Child</a>, and Zwentibold was later venerated locally as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zwentibold.jpg" alt="Zwentibold" width="244" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ekkehard von Aura · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zwentibold-king.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
